## 5. Resolving the manifest.json "Error"
The JSON snippet you pasted:
```json
{
  "manifest_version": 3,
  "name": "ChromeOS Location Tracker",
  "version": "1.0",
  "description": "Enterprise extension to track managed ChromeOS device location.",
  "background": {
    "service_worker": "background.js"
  },
  "permissions": [
    "enterprise.deviceAttributes",
    "offscreen",
    "alarms",
    "geolocation"
  ],
  "host_permissions": [
    "http://localhost:8080/*",
    "https://*.yourdomain.com/*"
  ]
}
```
**This is completely valid.** If you are seeing a red syntax error in your code editor, it is simply because **you are missing the final closing brace `}`** at the very bottom of the file. Ensure the file ends with a `}` and the error will disappear!

